  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/bengaluru\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bengaluru</a>: A city hospital has become the fastest in the country to complete <a href=\"/tag/3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3</a>,<a href=\"/tag/000+robot-assisted+surgeries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">000 robot-assisted surgeries</a> using the <a href=\"/tag/da+vinci+xi+surgical+system\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Da Vinci Xi surgical system</a>. The milestone was achieved by Fortis Hospital, Bannerghatta Road, eight years after it launched the programme in 2018, the hospital said Saturday.The hospital said it has performed robotic surgeries across 12 specialties, including urology, <a href=\"/tag/kidney+transplantation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">kidney transplantation</a>, gynaecology, surgical oncology, gastrointestinal, bariatric, and cardiac surgery. It also said it is among the few hospitals in India with two Da Vinci Xi robotic surgical systems under one roof and has launched the country’s first Total Robot Enabled and Assisted Transplant (TREAT) programme for kidney transplants.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>Speaking at the event, the state health minister, UT Khader said, “Karnataka has built a strong reputation as a centre of excellence in healthcare, driven by clinical expertise, innovation, and a steadfast commitment to patient care. As medical technology continues to evolve, our priority must be to ensure that innovation translates into safer care, better access and improved outcomes for patients.”</p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                    \n\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Aug 3, 2026 at 06:57 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Aug 3, 2026 at 06:57 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel